.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
*.log

# =============================================================================
# Bridge
# =============================================================================
# The bridge source IS tracked: it is on mainnet, it holds other people's money,
# and it went through three hardening rounds plus a route preflight. Untracked
# source for the most security-critical code in the project was the wrong trade.
#
# What stays out: build output, vendored dependencies, and anything holding a key.
bridge/**/node_modules/
bridge/contracts/out/
bridge/contracts/cache/
bridge/contracts/lib/
bridge/relayer/artifacts/
bridge/relayer/state/
bridge/ui/dist/
bridge/watcher/watcher.state.json
bridge/watcher/watcher.state.json.tmp

# Rehearsal keystores sit next to their own password files. They are devnet-only,
# but a keystore committed beside its password teaches the habit that loses a
# mainnet key, so they never enter history.
bridge/rehearsal/keys/

# The real relayer config carries per-host bearer tokens; only the examples ship.
bridge/relayer/config/chains.json

# Rendered docs output (built by docs/build-docs.mjs)
docs/dist/

# Release artifacts: the binaries and archives are reproducible from the tagged
# source and are far too large for history. SHA256SUMS and the README — how
# each platform was built and what was NOT verified — are tracked.
infra/release/*/bin/
infra/release/*/*.tar.gz
infra/release/*/*.zip

# Lab rehearsal runtime: generated lab keys, cloned datadirs, per-run state.
# Lab-only keys, but a keystore committed beside its password teaches the habit
# that loses a mainnet key. Scripts and evidence are tracked; .run is not.
infra/lab/.run/

# superseded release artefacts kept for the record, never published
infra/release/*/.superseded-*/

# Lab evidence is the PROOF behind ticked runbook items, not incidental output.
# The blanket *.log rule silently excluded it, so citations in RELEASE-posa.md
# pointed at files that were never committed and three others survived only
# because someone remembered `git add -f`. Evidence is tracked by default now.
!infra/lab/evidence/
!infra/lab/evidence/*.log

# =============================================================================
# PUBLIC-RELEASE REDACTIONS (2026-09-22)
# The repo is published at github.com/aliasghar89/ferminux. These files stay on
# the operator's disk and out of the published tree: they map the authority set
# to physical hosts, or they are build output that does not belong in git.
# =============================================================================
# Validator placement runbook: signer -> host -> provider, plus each host's
# known weak point and the key-escrow procedure. An attacker's target list for
# a five-signer PoA chain. Operator-only.
infra/RELEASE-posa.md
# Lab devnet P2P node private keys (networkid 39610). Lab-only, no funds, but
# a keystore in git teaches the habit that loses a mainnet key.
infra/lab/.run/
# Compiled stratum proxy binary (8.4 MB). Reproducible from proxy/ source.
proxy/stratum-proxy
